{
  "id": "i02-l03",
  "unit": "i02-and-then",
  "title": "Happy to hear it",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The participle can give the **cause** of a feeling: **শুনে খুশি হলাম** 'I was glad to hear it' (lit. having heard, I became glad).\n\n- **দেখে ভয় পেলাম** 'I got scared when I saw it'\n- **শুনে অবাক হলাম** 'I was surprised to hear it'\n\nSome feelings take **হলাম** 'I became': **খুশি হলাম**, **অবাক হলাম**, **বিরক্ত হলাম**. Others take **পেলাম** 'I got': **ভয় পেলাম**, **কষ্ট পেলাম**.\n\n**হেসে** 'smiling, with a laugh' and **রেগে** 'angrily' say how someone did something: **সে রেগে চলে গেল**.\n\n**কী খবর?** is the everyday 'What's up?'",
